# 033 — 8×16 font with Cyrillic and box drawing — done

**Type:** feature · **Priority:** P0 · **Status:** done (2026-10-04) · **Blocked by:** — · **Roadmap:** track G, tools plan F2

## Problem

`common/font.rs` has 64 glyphs (ASCII 32–95): no lower case, no Cyrillic, no box-drawing or block characters. Text tools need all of them; the UI must be English and Russian (track G).

## Plan

- Take a free font: Terminus 4.49.1 (`ter-u16n.bdf`, 8×16, SIL OFL 1.1, © Dimitar Toshkov Zhekov). The OFL allows embedding with software; a subset is a modified version and may not use the reserved name "Terminus Font", so the subset is called **MIND Mono 16** and keeps the copyright and the licence.
- `scripts/font_gen.py`: `--subset <bdf>` writes the subset `fonts/mind-mono-16.bdf` (ASCII, Latin-1, Cyrillic U+0400–U+045F and U+0490–U+0491, general punctuation, arrows, №, box drawing U+2500–U+257F, block elements U+2580–U+259F, geometric shapes, U+FFFD); without arguments it generates `common/font16.rs` from the subset; `--check` fails if the generated file is stale.
- `common/font16.rs`: sorted code points and 16-byte bitmaps, `glyph(char) -> &[u8; 16]` (binary search; ASCII directly; unknown → U+FFFD).
- `fonts/OFL.txt` and `fonts/README.md`: origin, version, SHA-256 of the source archive, what was changed.
- `mind::gfx::Screen::text16` draws UTF-8 text with it.

## Acceptance criteria

- Generator freshness test; host test that every subset range is present and lookup works.
- A screendump shows Cyrillic and box drawing drawn by a program.

## Related

[docs/tools](../docs/tools/README.md) F2, [issue 009](../issues/009-gop-pixel-format.md).

## Resolution

`fonts/mind-mono-16.bdf`: 775 glyphs of Terminus Font 4.49.1 (`ter-u16n.bdf`, archive SHA-256 recorded in `fonts/README.md`) — ASCII, Latin-1, Cyrillic with Ґ/ґ, punctuation, €, №, ™, arrows, math signs, box drawing, block elements, geometric shapes, check marks, braille patterns (2×4 dots for graphs), U+FFFD. Under the OFL the subset is a modified version, so it is named MIND Mono; the copyright and `fonts/OFL.txt` are kept. `scripts/font_gen.py` makes the subset and the generated `common/font16.rs` (sorted code points, 16-byte rows, `glyph()` by binary search with an ASCII fast path, `has()`); `libmind` exports it as `mind::font16`, and `Screen::glyph16`/`text16` draw UTF-8 text. `tests/font_test.py` checks coverage, cell size, the licence notice and freshness. The `files` demo draws a title with Cyrillic, an em dash and box drawing; the `services` QEMU suite compares it with the font bitmaps pixel for pixel.

Correction (with 034): the default Terminus glyphs of в, д, и, й are Bulgarian forms (и looks like u, д like g); the subset is now built after the font's own variant patches `alt/dv1.diff` and `alt/ij1.diff`, which give the Russian forms. `tests/font_test.py` checks it.
